<div class="h-[695px] sm:h-[565px] relative h-[565px] md:h-[275px] absolute top-20 pb-4 flex gap-4 flex-row flex-wrap w-full   overflow-auto ">
  
    <kbd class="kbd right-52 top-1 absolute text-cyan-800 bg-gradient-to-t from-sky-100 to-cyan-100 rounded-sm">BEAST MODE</kbd>
    <p class="right-5 top-1 absolute bg-gradient-to-t from-teal-900 to-sky-900 bg-clip-text text-transparent">@(new DateTime(2025, 7, 31, 10, 0, 0).ToString("MMMM dd, yyyy – hh:mm tt"))</p>
    <button type="submit" class=" btn right-24 top-10 absolute bg-gradient-to-t from-teal-400 to-cyan-500 text-cyan-100 rounded-md">Modify</button>
    <input type="checkbox" aria-label="Ended" class=" btn right-5 top-10 absolute bg-gradient-to-t from-green-400 to-emerald-500 text-cyan-100 rounded-md" style="border-bottom: solid 1px rgba(0, 177, 191)"/>
    <h1 class="inline-block max-w-[90%] mt-27 ml-7 text-lg break-words italic font-semibold bg-gradient-to-t from-cyan-900 to-sky-900 bg-clip-text text-transparent">
        The Sin That Knows My Name
    </h1>

   <div class="flex justify-center ">
        <p class=" mb-55 sm:mt-5 text-justify mt-5 overflow-auto  h-[440px] w-[95%] font-semilight bg-gradient-to-t from-cyan-800 to-sky-900 bg-clip-text text-transparent indent-6
">
            He never had to look for it. The sin always found him.

            It waited patiently in the silence between prayers, in the pause before sleep, in the breath before he said no—but meant yes.

            He knew its shape. It didn’t wear horns or carry smoke. It was familiar. Gentle. Sometimes it even looked like comfort.

            Each time he turned away from it, he found it already ahead of him, smiling, as if to say: “We both know you’ll come back.”

            And he did.

            He would fall to his knees and curse his weakness. Swear it was the last time. Yet when the moment returned, he would greet it like an old friend.

            “What power do you hold over me?” he asked once in the dark.

            The sin whispered, “None. You keep calling me.”

            He never forgot that voice. It was soft. And it knew his name.
        </p>
   </div>
</div>

